# PoCol Studio, IDE & Viewer: the release manifest public key (SITES-PLAN W14, Q7), the owner's, committed 2026-11-18.
#
# Chrome derives the extension id from the manifest "key" (sha256 of this DER SubjectPublicKeyInfo), so every release
# built with it has one fixed id: users compare it with the id published on pocol.net, and Chrome keeps the extension's
# storage (the studio:wallet vault) across releases loaded from any folder.
#
# The line below is the base64 DER SubjectPublicKeyInfo of the owner's RSA 2048 release manifest key, on one line (the
# public half only; the private key never enters this repository). It was made offline with:
#   openssl genrsa -out KEY.pem 2048
#   openssl rsa -in KEY.pem -pubout -outform DER | base64 -w0
# `python3 scripts/package-release.py --extension-id` prints the id to publish:
#   gggcoflmedlhlkcdhebmoepmggdnafmp
#
# node build.mjs builds dist/ with this manifest "key". Fault, testGateway and rehearsal builds never carry the key, so
# loading one never replaces a release install.

